# Environment contract. These are the ONLY things that differ per deployment
# and the only things that live in Vercel env vars. Everything else (active
# spreadsheet ID, rooms/timeslots, proctor allowlist) is configured in-app by a
# superuser and stored in the app's own backend, so the QA deployment simply
# gets pointed at the QA spreadsheet from the setup screen.
#
# Copy to .env.local for local overrides (gitignored). Secrets are read lazily
# by src/lib/env.ts, so a missing value fails the first request that needs it
# rather than the build. The home page shows which ones are present.
#
# Nothing here may be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.

# qa | prod. Defaults to qa via the committed .env; only the Prod Vercel project sets prod.
# APP_ENV=qa

# Google OAuth 2.0 client (type: Web application) used for sign-in and for the
# Sheets write as the TA. Separate clients for QA and Prod so the QA client can
# stay in Google's Testing status. Mark the secret as Sensitive in Vercel.
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Signs session cookies. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# Use a different value per deployment.
# AUTH_SECRET=

# Comma-separated Andrew IDs of head TAs who may edit the setup screen
# (active sheet, rooms, proctor allowlist). Everyone else is read-only there.
# SUPERUSERS=headta,anotherta

# Only for running a production build locally with `pnpm start`. Never needed
# in `pnpm dev` or on Vercel.
# AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true
